
This is a fork of the Sshd4a Android SSH server (dropbear + rsync + sftp-server)
with extra login roles, a small package manager and helper commands.

COMMANDS
  help, sshd4a help       this text
  version, ver            print the app version
  sshd4a env [--file]     print shell code that adds Sshd4a's bin dir to PATH
                          (--file: print the path of the equivalent file)
  pkg                     package manager (see below)
  termux, tmx             enter the Termux environment (see below)
  tmux                    terminal multiplexer, per-role alias (see below)

LOGIN ROLES (set a login/password per role in the app's Settings)
  user    the app's own sandbox uid; prompt ends with  $
  shell   uid 2000 (adb shell), via su;                 prompt ends with  şҥ
  root    uid 0, via su;                                prompt ends with  #

SWITCHING USERS (inside a session; uses the system su)
  su, su root, su r       become root
  su shell, su s          become shell (uid 2000)
  su user, su u           become the app's own user (sandbox)
  su <uid> ...            anything else goes to the system su unchanged

FILES AND FOLDERS (/data/local/tmp/Sshd4a)
  bin/                    pkg-installed tools and the commands above
  etc/                    configuration (below)      tmp/   shared /tmp (1777)
  root/home, shell/home   home folders of the root and shell roles
  etc/bashrc-common       edit freely: aliases for root AND shell (created once)
  etc/custom-root         edit freely: extras for root only (created once)
  etc/custom-shell        edit freely: extras for shell only (created once)
  etc/tmux.conf           shared tmux config (created once)
  etc/pkg-repos.list      package repo list (created once; use `pkg repo`)
  etc/rc-root rc-shell rc-user rc-lib rc-termux env termux-info
                          regenerated on every service start / settings save:
                          do not edit (put your changes in the files above;
                          the user role also reads  ~/.shrc-user  if present)

TMUX
  `tmux` is an alias that always passes a per-role socket (tmux-root.sock,
  tmux-shell.sock, tmux-user.sock) and etc/tmux.conf. Roles do not share
  sessions: a session started as root is not visible to shell.

AUTOSTART
  Every role has a folder  ~/autostart.d  (root/home, shell/home, and the
  app's own home for the user role). Each time the service starts, the files
  in it are run in name order, in the background, as that role, with
  `sh <file>` (so they need no exec permission). Output is appended to
  ~/autostart.log.
  Scripts start asynchronously: each one is put in the background and the next
  starts immediately, without waiting for the previous one to finish. A
  long-running script (a daemon) therefore never blocks the others; name order
  only decides the start order. If one script must wait for another, call them
  one after the other from a single script. Scripts run again on every service
  restart, so make them safe to run twice (check whether the daemon is already
  running).

TERMUX
  `termux` or `tmx` enters Termux's own login environment (needs root/su for
  now). If Termux is not installed, or comes from Google Play (a separate,
  unsupported build), it says so and points to F-Droid / GitHub. Termux is
  detected at service start; restart the service after installing it.
  Not implemented yet: non-root access (Termux RUN_COMMAND).

EXTERNAL TERMINALS / APPS
  . /data/local/tmp/Sshd4a/etc/env      add Sshd4a's tools to PATH
  eval "$(sshd4a env)"                  the same, without sourcing a file
  It only changes PATH (it will not break Termux's own HOME/TMPDIR).
  The calling app must be able to read and execute files there.

STARTING / STOPPING FROM OUTSIDE (adb shell, Termux, scripts)
  Enable "Allow starting the service by an external Intent" in Settings first.
  The package is com.roshkond.sshd4a.extended; the original Sshd4a answers the
  same actions, so always name the component. Headless (no app window):
    am broadcast -n com.roshkond.sshd4a.extended/com.hardbacknutter.sshd.ControlReceiver -a com.hardbacknutter.sshd.fg.START
    (same with ...fg.STOP)  -> prints result=<code>, data="<message>":
    1 done, 2 nothing to do, 3 option disabled, 4 failed (see data), 5 stop refused
  With the app window (activity):
    am start -n com.roshkond.sshd4a.extended/com.hardbacknutter.sshd.MainActivity -a com.hardbacknutter.sshd.fg.START
  Running a command (needs "Allow external command execution"; exec_as =
  root|shell|user, optional --es token):
    am broadcast -n com.roshkond.sshd4a.extended/com.hardbacknutter.sshd.ExecReceiver -a com.hardbacknutter.sshd.fg.EXEC --es cmd "id" --es exec_as root
  More: docs/EXTERNAL-RUN.md in the repository.

PACKAGE MANAGER (pkg)
  pkg update                  refresh the package index from all repos
  pkg list                    packages available for this device's CPU
  pkg installed               installed packages
  pkg install [--force] NAME  download, verify sha256, install into bin/
                              (without --force it will not shadow a tool the
                              system already provides)
  pkg remove NAME             remove an installed package
  pkg repo list               configured repos
  pkg repo add URL            add your own repo (an index file URL)
  pkg repo remove URL         remove a repo
  Index line format (one per package, '#' = comment):
    name|arch|version|url|sha256|install_name
  The default repo is built from bnsmb/binaries-for-Android (arm64 only) plus
  this project's own bash builds. Downloads use busybox wget.
